WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.780
- Hi, welcome back to the Lam Rim.

00:00:02.780 --> 00:00:06.130
We're going to explain
this mysterious photo

00:00:06.130 --> 00:00:09.840
as we go through the class
and let's go to the Tibetan.

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:12.733
The name of this class by
the way, of this session,

00:00:12.733 --> 00:00:15.240
is called, We Never Know Who People Are.

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:17.718
And here's the Tibetan of the Lam Rim.

00:00:17.718 --> 00:00:18.800
'DI BSGOM PA NA

00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:22.520
If you keep up this meditation
that I asked you to treasure

00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:27.520
and not lose the tradition
that I worked so hard to get,

00:00:29.583 --> 00:00:31.782
DANG POR TSE 'DI' AA
MAS SKYE BA SNGA MA'I MA

00:00:31.782 --> 00:00:33.420
MANG DU BYAS PAR BSGOM

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:36.710
start with your mom in this life

00:00:36.710 --> 00:00:39.380
and think about how many past lives

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:43.020
she was your mom, over and over.

00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:47.550
Then, now we expand and we have a picture

00:00:47.550 --> 00:00:50.650
of an expanding circle of water.

00:00:50.650 --> 00:00:55.610
Think about: now expand the vision,

00:00:55.610 --> 00:00:58.490
like the ripples in a pond

00:00:58.490 --> 00:01:03.010
when you drop a stone in the middle.

00:01:03.010 --> 00:01:05.250
Expand it to your dad.

00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:07.160
Expand it to your father in this life.

00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:12.160
My dad in this life has been
my mom in countless lives.

00:01:14.690 --> 00:01:16.283
So expand it to your father.

00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:19.910
Start with your mom in this life,

00:01:19.910 --> 00:01:23.040
Imagine that she's been
your mom countless times.

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:25.186
Then when you're ready,
expand it to your father.

00:01:25.186 --> 00:01:26.500
PHA LA BSGOM

00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:29.283
Expand the meditation to your father.

00:01:29.283 --> 00:01:30.838
DE NAS GNYEN GZHAN DANG

00:01:30.838 --> 00:01:32.930
Then expand it to other relatives:

00:01:32.930 --> 00:01:36.403
uncles, aunts, grandparents, whatever.

00:01:37.880 --> 00:01:40.419
Then, DE NAS BAR MA

00:01:40.419 --> 00:01:43.490
Then go to people that you don't know.

00:01:43.490 --> 00:01:44.817
People you've never met.

00:01:44.817 --> 00:01:46.560
I don't know.

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:48.294
I have some neighbors in my neighborhood

00:01:48.294 --> 00:01:50.350
that I have never talked to them.

00:01:50.350 --> 00:01:53.130
I like them, I mean,
we smiled at each other

00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:55.620
but they're not relatives.

00:01:55.620 --> 00:01:58.714
They're just kind of
neutral people in my life.

00:01:58.714 --> 00:02:00.280
DE DAG LA MNYONG BA LEGS PAR THON

00:02:00.280 --> 00:02:01.750
MNYONG BA THON

00:02:01.750 --> 00:02:04.257
means you got good at it.

00:02:04.257 --> 00:02:07.710
It means experience has flowed out.

00:02:07.710 --> 00:02:11.900
It's an idiom in Tibetan
that means once you get good

00:02:11.900 --> 00:02:15.065
at working on your mom and your dad

00:02:15.065 --> 00:02:16.470
and then other relatives

00:02:16.470 --> 00:02:19.600
and people you don't know much about,

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:23.365
then you're ready for DGRA, Tim?

00:02:23.365 --> 00:02:25.198
DGRA BCOM PA

00:02:28.086 --> 00:02:29.905
- [Student] For?

00:02:29.905 --> 00:02:30.738
- Enemy.

00:02:30.738 --> 00:02:32.000
- [Student] Enemy.
- Yeah.

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:35.400
Then you're ready for your enemies.

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:39.530
It's called Ari in Sanskrit, Ari Hat,

00:02:39.530 --> 00:02:41.673
means enemy destroyer.

00:02:43.249 --> 00:02:44.082
So DGRA LA DMIGS NAS

00:02:44.082 --> 00:02:45.690
Focus on your enemies.

00:02:45.690 --> 00:02:48.837
People you don't like and

00:02:48.837 --> 00:02:50.596
MA BYAS PAR BSAMS

00:02:50.596 --> 00:02:53.440
think about, this MA is not negative.

00:02:53.440 --> 00:02:57.023
It means they served as your mom

00:02:57.023 --> 00:02:57.856
MA BYAS PA

00:02:57.856 --> 00:03:00.450
They did your mom.

00:03:00.450 --> 00:03:01.327
Think about it.

00:03:01.327 --> 00:03:05.314
BSAMS RJES

00:03:05.314 --> 00:03:07.566
Until, BSAMS RJES means after that

00:03:07.566 --> 00:03:09.774
SEMS CAN THAMS CAD LA DMIGS TE SBYONG

00:03:09.774 --> 00:03:12.120
till you get to the point

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:14.450
where you can do it
towards all living beings.

00:03:14.450 --> 00:03:16.740
He doesn't mention animals and bugs

00:03:16.740 --> 00:03:20.022
but that's what SEMS CAN can mean

00:03:20.022 --> 00:03:22.350
in colloquial Tibetan.

00:03:22.350 --> 00:03:25.390
That's expanded to non-humans.

00:03:25.390 --> 00:03:28.635
All right, so this idea of
expanding the meditation.

00:03:28.635 --> 00:03:29.900
'O NA

00:03:29.900 --> 00:03:34.243
Now very interesting and famous objection.

00:03:35.870 --> 00:03:38.600
He's trying to sell us a car.

00:03:38.600 --> 00:03:40.942
Pabongka Rinpoche is
trying to sell us a car

00:03:40.942 --> 00:03:42.810
called MAR SHES,

00:03:42.810 --> 00:03:44.720
realize that everyone is your mom.

00:03:44.720 --> 00:03:47.690
Then in every sales pitch
there's objections, right?

00:03:47.690 --> 00:03:49.140
The customer makes objections.

00:03:49.140 --> 00:03:53.330
This car, there's not a lot of
electricity charging stations

00:03:53.330 --> 00:03:55.110
in the middle of Arizona.

00:03:55.110 --> 00:03:57.240
Then the salesman has to
come back and say, "No,

00:03:57.240 --> 00:03:59.913
but there's so many being put in!"

00:04:01.150 --> 00:04:05.498
So here's the objection from
the customer, which is us:

00:04:05.498 --> 00:04:07.870
MA YIN MA NGO SHES DGOS

00:04:07.870 --> 00:04:11.890
If someone were my mom, I would know.

00:04:11.890 --> 00:04:14.340
I would know, come on.

00:04:14.340 --> 00:04:19.320
If someone had spent 20,
30, 40 years feeding me,

00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:21.910
raising me, teaching me everything.

00:04:21.910 --> 00:04:24.690
Look, I'm not stupid.
I would recognize her.

00:04:24.690 --> 00:04:26.456
I would know.

00:04:26.456 --> 00:04:28.290
DGOS

00:04:28.290 --> 00:04:31.050
DE MI SHES PAS MA MIN NO SNYAM NA

00:04:31.050 --> 00:04:35.460
And since I don't
recognize these strangers

00:04:35.460 --> 00:04:39.180
have been my mom, they
have not been my mom.

00:04:39.180 --> 00:04:40.760
If they had been my mom,

00:04:40.760 --> 00:04:42.650
I would have this feeling towards them.

00:04:42.650 --> 00:04:44.400
I would feel the connection.

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:45.680
But I don't feel the connection.

00:04:45.680 --> 00:04:48.300
So I don't think they've been my mom.

00:04:48.300 --> 00:04:52.923
Then here comes Pabongka
Rinpoche salesman answer:

00:04:52.923 --> 00:04:56.356
SANGS RGYAS KYIS KYANG,
MA MA BYAS PA'I SEMS CAN

00:04:56.356 --> 00:04:58.150
GCIG KYANG MA GZIGS

00:04:58.150 --> 00:05:01.239
Even a Buddha is incapable

00:05:01.239 --> 00:05:04.970
of perceiving with their own eyes

00:05:04.970 --> 00:05:08.756
that anyone has not been their mother.

00:05:08.756 --> 00:05:11.880
MA MA BYAS

00:05:11.880 --> 00:05:13.663
Mother not done mother.

00:05:15.770 --> 00:05:20.610
Even a Buddha does not have the capacity

00:05:20.610 --> 00:05:24.643
to recognize that anyone
has not been their mother.

00:05:25.881 --> 00:05:27.964
RANG RES NGO MA SHES PA MA GTOGS

00:05:27.964 --> 00:05:30.222
MA DNGOS GNAS YIN TE

00:05:30.222 --> 00:05:31.740
Okay, I agree,

00:05:31.740 --> 00:05:34.180
You don't feel like they were your mom.

00:05:34.180 --> 00:05:37.080
You don't feel a connection
to them, I understand.

00:05:37.080 --> 00:05:39.570
But the Buddha does.

00:05:39.570 --> 00:05:42.720
The person who sees all
things, sees that connection.

00:05:42.720 --> 00:05:45.570
So I understand you don't
feel a connection like that.

00:05:45.570 --> 00:05:49.487
I understand, but you're
just stupid and wrong.

00:05:50.740 --> 00:05:54.657
Because Buddha who sees all things says,

00:05:54.657 --> 00:05:55.980
"They have been."

00:05:55.980 --> 00:05:59.990
So don't think that you're going to,

00:05:59.990 --> 00:06:03.180
if you don't have an emotional
connection to somebody

00:06:03.180 --> 00:06:04.993
they have never been your mother

00:06:06.150 --> 00:06:08.630
in the past life. Don't think like that.

00:06:08.630 --> 00:06:10.230
Looks can be deceiving.

00:06:10.230 --> 00:06:14.400
There are people who are,
people are not what they seem

00:06:14.400 --> 00:06:17.450
and people are not what they feel.

00:06:17.450 --> 00:06:20.583
And I like to give this
example of this next photo.

00:06:23.270 --> 00:06:26.920
So, here you see me with Venerable Jigme

00:06:26.920 --> 00:06:28.380
and my wife Veronica.

00:06:28.380 --> 00:06:33.380
We are giving a down payment
for this little tiny cafe

00:06:34.268 --> 00:06:38.940
we are buying from this couple.

00:06:38.940 --> 00:06:41.540
This couple is in their 70's.

00:06:41.540 --> 00:06:46.540
The lady whose name
is, nickname is Cricket

00:06:46.858 --> 00:06:49.933
because she's about this tall.

00:06:51.200 --> 00:06:55.890
When they were on their
honeymoon a 100 years ago,

00:06:55.890 --> 00:06:59.630
the guy who ran the
bed and breakfast said,

00:06:59.630 --> 00:07:02.677
told the husband, the new husband,

00:07:02.677 --> 00:07:04.380
"Hey, don't loose that cricket.

00:07:04.380 --> 00:07:05.970
Don't let that cricket
fall out of your bed,

00:07:05.970 --> 00:07:07.560
you're going to lose her."

00:07:07.560 --> 00:07:12.320
After that, they called the
cafe Crickets, after the wife.

00:07:12.320 --> 00:07:15.160
So she ran the cooking.
Can you keep it up?

00:07:16.068 --> 00:07:18.801
She ran the kitchen,

00:07:18.801 --> 00:07:22.723
and then he would, on the weekends,

00:07:22.723 --> 00:07:25.900
he would show up and
pour coffee for people.

00:07:25.900 --> 00:07:29.210
He would just say... He'd
come up, he's very shy

00:07:29.210 --> 00:07:32.990
and he'd say, "Would you
like some more coffee?"

00:07:32.990 --> 00:07:36.040
And I was talking to people,

00:07:36.040 --> 00:07:37.520
I used to hang out there,

00:07:37.520 --> 00:07:39.520
"Maybe he's retarded a little bit? Or..."

00:07:39.520 --> 00:07:44.050
It's just kind of, they
just gave him the coffee

00:07:44.050 --> 00:07:46.807
and said, "Ask people, do
they need more coffee?"

00:07:48.070 --> 00:07:50.080
Then later I found out

00:07:50.080 --> 00:07:53.373
he's one of the leading
astronomers in the world.

00:07:54.830 --> 00:07:59.830
He's been running the
observatory, Lowell Observatory

00:08:01.360 --> 00:08:03.720
where they discovered Pluto.

00:08:03.720 --> 00:08:07.270
He discovered the
atmosphere of Pluto himself,

00:08:07.270 --> 00:08:09.960
and he's tracking thousands of asteroids

00:08:09.960 --> 00:08:13.240
to make sure they don't
crash into this planet.

00:08:13.240 --> 00:08:15.893
And he invented the
systems for tracking them.

00:08:17.150 --> 00:08:18.320
Then I'm like suddenly,

00:08:18.320 --> 00:08:22.470
I'm like, "He's not this dull
guy who's pouring coffee,

00:08:22.470 --> 00:08:24.260
he's a world famous astronomer!"

00:08:24.260 --> 00:08:27.680
He's one of the greatest
astronomers alive today.

00:08:27.680 --> 00:08:31.380
What's the lesson here?

00:08:31.380 --> 00:08:34.620
Just because you don't
feel like he's a genius

00:08:34.620 --> 00:08:37.950
doesn't mean he's not a genius.

00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:41.830
Just because you don't feel
like someone is your mom,

00:08:41.830 --> 00:08:43.800
maybe your feelings are wrong.

00:08:43.800 --> 00:08:47.557
Maybe your impression of this guy is wrong

00:08:47.557 --> 00:08:50.440
and maybe he's not what you think he is.

00:08:50.440 --> 00:08:52.350
And the older you get in this life,

00:08:52.350 --> 00:08:54.050
Gyelse can tell you, right?

00:08:55.170 --> 00:08:58.197
The more you've realized
that you meet people

00:08:58.197 --> 00:09:03.197
and you're completely wrong about them.

00:09:03.240 --> 00:09:05.690
TSE 'DI'I MA YANG PHYIS
KHYI LTA BUR SKYES NAS

00:09:05.690 --> 00:09:08.960
YOD KYANG RANG GIS MI SHES

00:09:08.960 --> 00:09:13.960
Look, even the mother you had
in this life, we don't know

00:09:16.280 --> 00:09:17.770
what she will be in her next life.

00:09:17.770 --> 00:09:20.030
She could be a dog. We don't know.

00:09:20.030 --> 00:09:22.230
She could be your pet dog.

00:09:22.230 --> 00:09:24.730
Your pet dog could be your mother

00:09:24.730 --> 00:09:28.552
who died earlier in your
life. We don't know.

00:09:28.552 --> 00:09:31.050
LTA BUR SKYES NAS YOD
KYANG RANG GIS MI SHES

00:09:31.050 --> 00:09:33.700
Maybe you don't understand,
maybe you just don't know.

00:09:33.700 --> 00:09:36.400
TSE 'DI'I MA DNGOS GNAS PA YANG

00:09:36.400 --> 00:09:38.541
NGO MI SHES PA YOD PA

00:09:38.541 --> 00:09:40.600
TSE 'DI'I MA

00:09:40.600 --> 00:09:41.566
And you have to read,

00:09:41.566 --> 00:09:43.923
Tim you have to read DNGOS GNAS PA

00:09:43.923 --> 00:09:44.948
DNGOS GNAS PA goes together.

00:09:44.948 --> 00:09:46.040
DNGOS GNAS PA

00:09:46.040 --> 00:09:48.080
And DNGOS GNAS PA means the real one,

00:09:48.080 --> 00:09:49.662
the genuine one.

00:09:49.662 --> 00:09:51.420
It's an idiom.

00:09:51.420 --> 00:09:54.720
DNGOS GNAS PA means the real one

00:09:54.720 --> 00:09:58.460
So even there's cases where people

00:09:58.460 --> 00:10:00.730
get separated from their mother

00:10:00.730 --> 00:10:03.800
and they don't even recognize
them when they meet them.

00:10:03.800 --> 00:10:08.670
Like this person, I
recently heard about a lady

00:10:08.670 --> 00:10:12.130
who gave up her daughter for adoption

00:10:12.130 --> 00:10:15.980
or her son for adoption,
when her son was born,

00:10:15.980 --> 00:10:17.370
and later they met each other

00:10:17.370 --> 00:10:18.480
and they used to hang out together

00:10:18.480 --> 00:10:20.780
and they didn't know
they were mother and son.

00:10:22.120 --> 00:10:22.960
They just didn't know.

00:10:22.960 --> 00:10:24.360
Then suddenly they figured it out,

00:10:24.360 --> 00:10:27.740
they were, "Oh my God...", so it happens.

00:10:27.740 --> 00:10:29.350
If your mom died in this life,

00:10:29.350 --> 00:10:31.830
she could be born as a dog, as your dog.

00:10:31.830 --> 00:10:35.250
And you wouldn't know, and you
wouldn't have that feeling.

00:10:35.250 --> 00:10:38.510
There is even people who
get separated from their mom

00:10:38.510 --> 00:10:40.326
in this life who later meet their mom,

00:10:40.326 --> 00:10:41.592
and don't recognize her.

00:10:41.592 --> 00:10:44.392
So don't think you have to recognize her.

00:10:44.392 --> 00:10:48.490
DGE SLONG MA AUTPA LA'I
MDOG GI LO RGYUS DANG

00:10:48.490 --> 00:10:53.490
Think about the story of
the nun called Utpala Varna,

00:10:53.645 --> 00:10:57.890
which means the color of the Blue Lotus.

00:10:57.890 --> 00:10:59.970
The lovely Blue Lotus.

00:10:59.970 --> 00:11:02.860
And there's a nun by this name.

00:11:02.860 --> 00:11:04.543
Think about this story of

00:11:04.543 --> 00:11:08.156
PHA SHA ZA ZHING MA LA 'TSOG

00:11:08.156 --> 00:11:10.075
That's a piece of a poem.

00:11:11.485 --> 00:11:14.685
PHA SHA ZA ZHING MA LA 'TSOG

00:11:14.685 --> 00:11:17.670
PHA SHA ZA ZHING MA LA 'TSOG

00:11:17.670 --> 00:11:21.860
And it's part of a longer
poem that is a sutra.

00:11:21.860 --> 00:11:23.857
The part here says,

00:11:23.857 --> 00:11:26.530
"This guy is eating his father's flesh

00:11:26.530 --> 00:11:29.130
and beating his mom on the head,

00:11:29.130 --> 00:11:31.810
smacking his mom on the head."

00:11:31.810 --> 00:11:34.360
'TSOG means, different spelling,

00:11:34.360 --> 00:11:36.530
it means smacking.

00:11:36.530 --> 00:11:38.900
You guys know the story, right?

00:11:38.900 --> 00:11:43.110
So a family lived next to a pond.

00:11:43.110 --> 00:11:46.520
The father used to catch
fishes there all the time.

00:11:46.520 --> 00:11:48.700
He used to eat the fish.

00:11:48.700 --> 00:11:53.593
Later... and the mom was
very attached to the house.

00:11:54.810 --> 00:11:56.870
Then they both died.

00:11:56.870 --> 00:11:59.310
They had kids and they died.

00:11:59.310 --> 00:12:00.760
They had a son and they died.

00:12:00.760 --> 00:12:02.260
Then the father was reborn

00:12:02.260 --> 00:12:05.890
as a fish in the pond, behind the house.

00:12:05.890 --> 00:12:08.127
We had the story in the Lam Rim.

00:12:08.127 --> 00:12:10.970
We gave you the whole story.

00:12:10.970 --> 00:12:14.170
The mom died and was born as a dog

00:12:14.170 --> 00:12:16.630
who was owned by the son,

00:12:16.630 --> 00:12:18.290
and the dog was attached to the house

00:12:18.290 --> 00:12:21.330
and used to growl at anybody
who would come in the house,

00:12:21.330 --> 00:12:24.360
because in the past life,

00:12:24.360 --> 00:12:27.790
the dog had been the mom who
was attached to the house.

00:12:27.790 --> 00:12:32.790
Then the guy gets married.

00:12:34.070 --> 00:12:36.070
He has the dog.

00:12:36.070 --> 00:12:39.640
He's still fishing out back,
the lake behind the house,

00:12:39.640 --> 00:12:41.270
the pond behind the house.

00:12:41.270 --> 00:12:44.500
He is catching his father sometimes

00:12:44.500 --> 00:12:46.520
and eating him at dinner.

00:12:46.520 --> 00:12:48.650
Then the father dies again.

00:12:48.650 --> 00:12:50.860
Then the father is born in the pond again.

00:12:50.860 --> 00:12:52.580
Then the son catches another fish,

00:12:52.580 --> 00:12:54.290
and that's a father again.

00:12:54.290 --> 00:12:55.620
Then he eats that fish.

00:12:55.620 --> 00:12:58.556
Now on top of all that,

00:13:00.660 --> 00:13:03.710
there is a guy who is
attracted to his wife

00:13:03.710 --> 00:13:06.200
and has an affair with his wife,

00:13:06.200 --> 00:13:08.690
and he goes and kills the guy.

00:13:08.690 --> 00:13:10.730
Because the guy was attracted

00:13:10.730 --> 00:13:12.500
to his wife's sexual organs,

00:13:12.500 --> 00:13:17.500
he's born in the wife's
womb and he's their son.

00:13:19.530 --> 00:13:23.680
So, basically this guy is
eating his, when he's at dinner

00:13:23.680 --> 00:13:27.190
the dog's trying to get
the fish off the plate

00:13:27.190 --> 00:13:30.700
and he's beating the dog,
smacking the dog on the head,

00:13:30.700 --> 00:13:34.210
which is his mom. And
he's eating his father.

00:13:34.210 --> 00:13:38.490
And he's hugging the guy who
had adultery with his wife,

00:13:38.490 --> 00:13:41.420
on his lap, who is his son.

00:13:41.420 --> 00:13:44.430
Then is it Maudgalyayana goes

00:13:44.430 --> 00:13:48.680
and asks for some leftovers
for his begging bowl.

00:13:48.680 --> 00:13:50.830
And the guy says, get
the hell out of here.

00:13:51.894 --> 00:13:55.370
Then another monk comes over and says,

00:13:55.370 --> 00:13:57.810
"You have no idea who is Maudgalyayana,

00:13:57.810 --> 00:14:01.180
he can travel to 1,000 planets for dinner.

00:14:01.180 --> 00:14:04.610
He doesn't need your food.
He's trying to help you."

00:14:04.610 --> 00:14:07.540
By the way, and then
he tells him the story

00:14:07.540 --> 00:14:10.040
of what's going on in his house.

00:14:10.040 --> 00:14:11.950
So we don't always recognize

00:14:11.950 --> 00:14:16.650
who the people around us
have been in the past.

00:14:16.650 --> 00:14:20.420
There's all kinds of people in our lives

00:14:20.420 --> 00:14:22.300
who might be people we knew before.

00:14:22.300 --> 00:14:26.612
I've met people I thought were
my mom, and stuff like that.

00:14:26.612 --> 00:14:29.500
We don't know. We don't really know.

00:14:29.500 --> 00:14:33.540
Alright, now the story
about the nun named Utpala

00:14:33.540 --> 00:14:36.440
is fascinating for me

00:14:36.440 --> 00:14:39.960
because we have a nun named
Utpala, who we love very much.

00:14:39.960 --> 00:14:42.940
And as I said, I don't know the story.

00:14:42.940 --> 00:14:45.970
I went and found the story
for you guys, which is my job

00:14:45.970 --> 00:14:47.960
And I enjoy that job.

00:14:47.960 --> 00:14:52.960
AI went and found the story
of the Blue Lotus, Utpala,

00:14:53.070 --> 00:14:55.310
and here's a blue lotus picture for you,

00:14:55.310 --> 00:14:58.210
just to get in the mood.

00:14:58.210 --> 00:15:00.424
She's called Utpala Varna.

00:15:00.424 --> 00:15:05.424
I found the story in a sutra called

00:15:05.497 --> 00:15:09.490
MDO MDZANGS BLUN

00:15:09.490 --> 00:15:13.750
Say MDO MDZANGS BLUN

00:15:13.750 --> 00:15:15.400
I love the name of the sutra

00:15:15.400 --> 00:15:20.400
because it means the Sutra
of the Wise and Foolish.

00:15:20.940 --> 00:15:25.360
The Sutra called Wise People and Fools,

00:15:25.360 --> 00:15:26.690
which is such a beautiful name.

00:15:26.690 --> 00:15:31.060
I mean, it would make a
good name for any book.

00:15:31.060 --> 00:15:34.280
So I read the story, it's extremely old.

00:15:34.280 --> 00:15:36.330
As apparently the sutra is very, very old

00:15:37.356 --> 00:15:39.460
and it was difficult to read.

00:15:39.460 --> 00:15:42.630
A couple of times I stopped
and I said, "It's too much,

00:15:42.630 --> 00:15:45.470
I don't have time to try
to figure out the story."

00:15:45.470 --> 00:15:47.510
But I worked it through

00:15:47.510 --> 00:15:49.450
and I'd like to teach it to you guys.

00:15:49.450 --> 00:15:52.790
It's worth it, it's worth it.

00:15:52.790 --> 00:15:55.348
So here we go.

00:16:02.700 --> 00:16:05.360
By the way, her story
was summarized briefly

00:16:05.360 --> 00:16:08.740
in this Lam Rim before, but
I'm giving you the whole story.

00:16:08.740 --> 00:16:10.388
So here we go.

00:16:10.388 --> 00:16:11.221
'CI' PHYIR

00:16:11.221 --> 00:16:13.198
You got the 'CI' PHYIR?

00:16:13.198 --> 00:16:14.380
'CI' PHYIR DE DAG

00:16:14.380 --> 00:16:17.583
I'm sorry, let's start below that.

00:16:17.583 --> 00:16:18.990
DE NAS

00:16:18.990 --> 00:16:22.183
And then four paragraphs below.

00:16:23.366 --> 00:16:25.303
DE NAS DGE SLONG

00:16:27.300 --> 00:16:29.690
Mr. Tim, skip four lines down,

00:16:29.690 --> 00:16:31.070
Skip 4 paragraphs down.

00:16:31.070 --> 00:16:34.470
Yeah, DE NAS, 347

00:16:34.470 --> 00:16:35.303
Good, okay.

00:16:35.303 --> 00:16:36.769
DE NAS DGE SLONG MA DE DAG

00:16:36.769 --> 00:16:41.310
So this story begins with
a bunch of Buddhist nuns

00:16:41.310 --> 00:16:44.375
who approach a senior nun.

00:16:44.375 --> 00:16:45.234
DGE SLONG MA DE DAG

00:16:45.234 --> 00:16:46.519
DGE SLONG MA AUTPA LA'I MDOG

00:16:46.519 --> 00:16:48.694
GANG NA 'DUG PAR SONG NAS

00:16:48.694 --> 00:16:53.694
These other nuns went
to where the Blue Lotus,

00:16:53.930 --> 00:16:57.011
the nun named Blue lotus was sitting.

00:16:57.011 --> 00:16:58.294
SONG NAS DER PHYIN PA DANG

00:16:58.294 --> 00:17:00.545
AUTPA LA'I MDOG LA PHYAG 'TSAL

00:17:00.545 --> 00:17:03.167
They made prostration to Blue Lotus

00:17:04.420 --> 00:17:06.628
and CHOS BZHIN DU SNYUN GSOL NAS

00:17:06.628 --> 00:17:08.430
'DI SKAD CES SMRAS SO

00:17:08.430 --> 00:17:11.244
Then they paid respect to her properly

00:17:11.244 --> 00:17:12.860
CHOS BZHIN DU

00:17:12.860 --> 00:17:16.260
And they said, "We have
something to ask you."

00:17:16.260 --> 00:17:17.943
Next paragraph.

00:17:17.943 --> 00:17:20.584
BDAG CAG KHYIM NA MCHIS PA NA

00:17:20.584 --> 00:17:22.775
KHYIM GYI LAS KYIS BSLUS

00:17:23.848 --> 00:17:27.940
We tried the home life
and they cheated us,

00:17:27.940 --> 00:17:29.730
BSLUS means deceived us.

00:17:29.730 --> 00:17:34.730
We tried the wife thing and
it just didn't work out.

00:17:36.103 --> 00:17:38.147
BSLUS NAS, DA RAB TU BYUNG

00:17:38.147 --> 00:17:40.080
So we became ordained.

00:17:42.309 --> 00:17:45.405
YANG 'DOD PA'I DBANG DU GYUR NAS

00:17:45.405 --> 00:17:47.880
But still we have
attractions to the home life,

00:17:47.880 --> 00:17:51.540
to sex, things like that, good clothes.

00:17:51.540 --> 00:17:55.420
We still are NYON MONGS
but, by those ideas,

00:17:55.420 --> 00:17:57.470
by those thoughts.

00:17:57.470 --> 00:18:02.143
So here's an ancient
verb, which is klesha-ed.

00:18:03.470 --> 00:18:06.500
We are still disturbed.

00:18:06.500 --> 00:18:09.160
Remember the definition of
a mental affliction, right?

00:18:09.160 --> 00:18:11.800
We are still disturbed
by thoughts of desire

00:18:11.800 --> 00:18:14.933
for house, husband, clothes.

00:18:16.702 --> 00:18:18.086
THAR PAR MI NUS

00:18:18.086 --> 00:18:19.960
We could not get over that.

00:18:19.960 --> 00:18:22.491
We could not moksha from that.

00:18:22.491 --> 00:18:24.070
BDAG CAG LA THUGS BRTZE BA'I SLAD DU

00:18:24.070 --> 00:18:26.574
If you love us,

00:18:26.574 --> 00:18:28.670
THUGS BRTZE BA, honorific,

00:18:28.670 --> 00:18:30.353
if you love us.

00:18:30.353 --> 00:18:31.750
DAM PA'I CHOS BSTAN DU GSOL

00:18:31.750 --> 00:18:33.160
please teach us the holy Dharma

00:18:33.160 --> 00:18:35.890
to help us fix this
condition of attachment

00:18:35.890 --> 00:18:39.349
to our old home life.

00:18:39.349 --> 00:18:40.695
AUTPA LAS SMRAS PA

00:18:40.695 --> 00:18:43.770
Then what do you want to
call it? Indigo Lotus?

00:18:43.770 --> 00:18:47.133
That's nice. Indigo answered them.

00:18:47.133 --> 00:18:50.483
KHYOD CI DANG CI 'DOD PA

00:18:50.483 --> 00:18:52.782
'DAS PA'AM MA 'ONGS PA'AM,
DA LTAR GYI DNGOS PO

00:18:52.782 --> 00:18:55.298
GANG YANG RUNG BA DRIS SHIG

00:18:55.298 --> 00:18:57.963
GNAS BSTAN PAR BYA'O

00:18:57.963 --> 00:19:00.130
Do you want me to talk
to you about situations

00:19:00.130 --> 00:19:01.920
that are in the past,

00:19:01.920 --> 00:19:03.610
or situations that happened in

00:19:03.610 --> 00:19:05.380
will happen in the future,

00:19:05.380 --> 00:19:08.090
or something that's going on nowadays?

00:19:08.090 --> 00:19:09.090
What's the context?

00:19:09.090 --> 00:19:11.240
Do you want a story from old days?

00:19:11.240 --> 00:19:12.900
Do you want a story from the future?

00:19:12.900 --> 00:19:16.040
By the way, at this point she was an arhat

00:19:16.040 --> 00:19:18.936
and there's a beautiful story
of her becoming an arhat.

00:19:18.936 --> 00:19:21.340
So she's an arhat and she's like,

00:19:21.340 --> 00:19:22.470
"You want me to tell the future?

00:19:22.470 --> 00:19:23.910
You want me to go over past?

00:19:23.910 --> 00:19:25.556
Which one do you want?"

00:19:25.556 --> 00:19:26.810
NGAS BSTAN PAR BYA'O

00:19:26.810 --> 00:19:30.470
I agree to teach you, but tell me what

00:19:30.470 --> 00:19:32.628
timeframe you guys are talking about?

00:19:32.628 --> 00:19:34.044
DGE SLONG MA RNAMS KYIS 'DAS PA DANG

00:19:34.044 --> 00:19:35.350
MA 'ONGS PA RE ZHIG ZHOG

00:19:35.350 --> 00:19:37.900
RE ZHIG ZHOG means let's forget the past

00:19:37.900 --> 00:19:41.020
and future for today.

00:19:41.020 --> 00:19:43.660
Just give us something going on now.

00:19:43.660 --> 00:19:46.620
Give us something that's
going on now that can help us

00:19:46.620 --> 00:19:50.120
get over our attachment
to the husbands and homes

00:19:50.120 --> 00:19:51.852
we used to have.

00:19:51.852 --> 00:19:54.603
BSTAN TE BDAG CAG GI
THE TSOM DGROL DU GSOL

00:19:54.603 --> 00:19:58.480
And we ask you to liberate our doubts.

00:19:58.480 --> 00:20:00.718
Free us from our doubts.

00:20:00.718 --> 00:20:02.250
AUTPA LAS SMRAS PA

00:20:02.250 --> 00:20:03.200
She answered,

00:20:03.200 --> 00:20:06.387
'DOD CHAGS NI, ME DANG 'DRA STE

00:20:06.387 --> 00:20:10.160
"Attachment to the worldly,
attachment to the home life

00:20:10.160 --> 00:20:14.742
is like a huge fire, huge wildfire."

00:20:14.742 --> 00:20:17.073
RI LUNG TSIG PAR BYED DO

00:20:17.073 --> 00:20:19.897
It can burn the mountains
and the valleys both.

00:20:21.113 --> 00:20:23.320
RTZA 'KHRI DANG 'DRA STE

00:20:23.320 --> 00:20:25.500
It's also like a family line

00:20:25.500 --> 00:20:28.903
in the sense that it's exponential.

00:20:31.110 --> 00:20:33.210
One person gives birth to a baby.

00:20:33.210 --> 00:20:37.670
That person has two babies.
Those babies have four babies,

00:20:37.670 --> 00:20:40.923
and desire tends to multiply upon itself.

00:20:42.083 --> 00:20:44.755
Here's the word for SKYE MCHED, Tim,

00:20:44.755 --> 00:20:47.596
in āyatana, in the Abhidharma.

00:20:47.596 --> 00:20:49.020
We call it door of sense,

00:20:49.020 --> 00:20:52.340
but it really means
exponential door of sense.

00:20:52.340 --> 00:20:57.050
One perception of an object
can lead to a 1,000 thoughts.

00:20:57.050 --> 00:21:00.590
'DOD CHAGS KYI DBANG GIS GCIG LA GCIG 'TSE

00:21:00.590 --> 00:21:02.360
Due to their attachment to things

00:21:02.360 --> 00:21:03.783
people hurt each other.

00:21:03.783 --> 00:21:05.984
GNOD PAR BYED - They do
damage to each other.

00:21:05.984 --> 00:21:09.350
DE LA YUN RING NA NGAN
SONG GSUM DU LHUNG STE

00:21:09.350 --> 00:21:12.470
If that goes on for any length of time

00:21:12.470 --> 00:21:15.490
then we fall into the three lower realms.

00:21:15.490 --> 00:21:16.740
THAR PA'I DUS MED DO

00:21:16.740 --> 00:21:20.140
It's almost impossible to free ourselves

00:21:20.140 --> 00:21:22.969
once we are in the lower realms.

00:21:22.969 --> 00:21:24.761
KHYIM NA GNAS PA NI

00:21:24.761 --> 00:21:27.277
SDUG PA LA CHAGS TE 'DOD PA DANG

00:21:28.294 --> 00:21:31.180
BYE BRAL BA DANG

00:21:31.180 --> 00:21:33.580
The definition of having
a home and a husband

00:21:33.580 --> 00:21:35.140
and all these things

00:21:35.140 --> 00:21:40.041
is almost like you are trying to

00:21:40.041 --> 00:21:42.500
practice attachment

00:21:42.500 --> 00:21:47.500
and the fear of disattachment,
the fear of losing things.

00:21:48.130 --> 00:21:50.380
By living the home life

00:21:50.380 --> 00:21:53.860
you are a study in attachment

00:21:53.860 --> 00:21:56.283
and the fears of losing what you have.

00:21:56.283 --> 00:21:58.025
SKYE BA DANG, RGA BA DANG,
NA BA DANG, 'CHI BA DANG

00:21:58.025 --> 00:21:59.541
RGYAL PO'I KHRIMS KYIS
GTZE BA'I SDUG BSNGAL

00:21:59.541 --> 00:22:00.680
RGYUN MI CHAD PAR MYONG STE

00:22:00.680 --> 00:22:04.146
It's a constant flow of

00:22:04.146 --> 00:22:08.662
rebirth, aging, illness, death,

00:22:10.240 --> 00:22:13.320
and the injustices of
the government, she says.

00:22:13.320 --> 00:22:15.080
I don't know why she threw that in there.

00:22:15.080 --> 00:22:19.050
That's probably close
to tax day or something.

00:22:19.050 --> 00:22:21.380
Injustices in the government.

00:22:21.380 --> 00:22:22.960
I don't know.

00:22:22.960 --> 00:22:27.054
I don't know there's probably
another sutra about that.

00:22:27.054 --> 00:22:30.387
TSE 'PHOS NAS PHYIR YANG SOS PA TZAM DU

00:22:32.560 --> 00:22:37.460
After you die, that
attachment to your house,

00:22:37.460 --> 00:22:40.400
to your home has other effects on you.

00:22:40.400 --> 00:22:42.963
The effects continue after you die.

00:22:44.373 --> 00:22:47.499
YANG SOS PA TZAM DU LUS

00:22:47.499 --> 00:22:51.100
He says, even if you just fall to the

00:22:51.100 --> 00:22:53.623
hell called Revive.

00:22:55.290 --> 00:22:58.610
So it's either a reference
to the hell called Revive

00:22:58.610 --> 00:23:02.630
or that those attachments
will revive themselves.

00:23:02.630 --> 00:23:06.223
They will come back to you. Either way,

00:23:07.290 --> 00:23:11.512
they will continue. The
repercussions of desire

00:23:11.512 --> 00:23:15.004
in this life continuing
into future life, GDUNGS TE

00:23:15.004 --> 00:23:15.910
SEMS GDUNGS

00:23:15.910 --> 00:23:17.831
They torture your mind

00:23:17.831 --> 00:23:20.764
KHYIM GYIS GLAGS SHING BCINGS PA NI

00:23:20.764 --> 00:23:23.170
BTZON RABS KYANG DAM MO

00:23:23.170 --> 00:23:25.190
To put it briefly,

00:23:25.190 --> 00:23:30.190
living in the home life for
a woman is like a prison.

00:23:30.610 --> 00:23:33.173
That's her final word on this.

00:23:34.360 --> 00:23:36.060
I want to stop there today.

00:23:36.060 --> 00:23:37.750
Tim and me agreed that would be nice

00:23:37.750 --> 00:23:41.593
to give you guys a break
sometimes, a shorter class.

00:23:43.274 --> 00:23:47.130
So we're going to stop that class there,

00:23:47.130 --> 00:23:48.770
and we'll be going on

00:23:48.770 --> 00:23:52.260
and continuing with the
story of Blue Lotus,

00:23:52.260 --> 00:23:55.550
this nun whose name is Blue Lotus.

00:23:55.550 --> 00:23:58.620
It's a story that you will never forget

00:23:58.620 --> 00:24:02.530
and that's the idea of putting
a story in the Lam Rim.

00:24:02.530 --> 00:24:04.800
See you in the next class.

